# Auto commit & push

When a coding task that changes the site is done (UI, data, scripts, styles):

1. Commit the relevant source changes (exclude `supabase/.temp/` and secrets).
2. Run `npm run build` so `docs/` stays in sync for GitHub Pages; include `docs/` in the same commit when the build succeeds.
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch.

Do **not** wait for the user to say “push” / 「推上 GitHub」 unless they asked only for a local change, or the push would be destructive (force-push, rewrite history).

If commit or push fails, fix what you can and report the blocker briefly.
